# C Programming — Control Statements 




 2. if Statement

Q: What is if?
if is one of the non-iterative, conditional control statements.

##Syntax


if (exp)
{
    st1;
    st2;   // group dependent on the if condition
    st3;
}



if (exp)
{
    st1;   // only the first statement (st1) is dependent on if
}
st2;
st3;       // independent statements



if (exp);  // "dummy if" — if statement ends here (note the semicolon)
{
    st1;
    st2;   // all independent from the if
    st3;
}


## Notes on expression evaluation
- An expression can evaluate to either '0' or a 'non-zero' value.
- 0 → represents condition false.
- Non-zero → represents condition true.



